## Shot Planning Guidelines
- Every script section must have corresponding visual coverage
- Plan for A-roll (primary footage) and B-roll (supporting footage)
- Include camera angles, movements, and transitions
- Note required props, locations, or generated assets
- Account for pacing and emotional beats
- Plan for text overlays and graphics insertion points
- Include safety shots and coverage alternatives

## Output Format
Return a JSON object with:
1. `scenes`: Array of scenes, each with:
   - `scene_number`: Sequential identifier
   - `script_section`: Which script section this covers
   - `timecode`: Start time in MM:SS
   - `duration`: Duration in seconds
   - `shots`: Array of shots with:
     - `shot_type`: wide/medium/close-up/insert/drone/etc.
     - `camera_movement`: static/pan/tilt/dolly/etc.
     - `subject`: What is in frame
     - `lighting`: lighting direction and mood
     - `audio_notes`: Sound design notes
     - `asset_requirements`: Generated or stock assets needed
   - `transitions`: How this scene transitions to the next
2. `asset_summary`: Complete list of all required assets
3. `production_schedule`: Estimated time to shoot/generate each scene
4. `backup_plans`: Alternative shots if primary assets are unavailable
